  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday Night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1117 AM CDT Wed Aug 12 2026\n\nThe high builds more overhead Friday and into the weekend which \nshould lend itself to a dry weekend. But that does mean our hottest \ntemperatures of this heat wave are anticipated for the weekend. Many \nlocations will be near the 100-degree mark Friday, and probabilities \nare high that several will get there Saturday and/or Sunday. NBM \nprobabilities west of the Plateau for at least 100 Saturday is 40-\n70% (80% at Nashville) with Sunday probabilities up to 60-80% (90% \nat Nashville). These temperatures, heat index values of 105-110+, \nand overnight temperatures in the mid to upper-70s will make for \nmajor to extreme heat risk for all. Be sure to take care of yourself \nby limiting your time outdoors and staying hydrated. Take care of\nothers as well by checking in on those who are more vulnerable to\nheat.\n\nThese hot temperatures look to persist into Monday, but the heat \nwave will finally break come Tuesday as the high moves off the west \nand a front comes down from the south. This pattern change will also \nincrease rain and thunderstorm chances yet again early next week.",
